---
import brand from '@arcvia/brand'
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro'
import plans from '@arcvia/brand/plans'
---

<Legal
  title="Refund policy"
  description={`Refunds and cancellations at ${brand.name}.`}
  updated="2026-08-18"
>
  {
    !plans.billingEnabled ? (
      <>
        <p>
          <strong>{brand.name} does not currently take payments.</strong> There
          is nothing to refund, no subscription to cancel and no card on file.
        </p>
        <p>
          This page exists because the policy below is what will apply the day
          billing is switched on, and it is fairer to publish it in advance than
          to produce it at the moment someone is first asked to pay.
        </p>
        <h2>What applies today</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Every feature is available at no cost.</li>
          <li>
            Credits meter GPU usage only. Running out is not a payment prompt.
          </li>
          <li>
            You can export your models and renders and leave at any time,
            without asking us.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <h2 id="when-billing-starts">When billing starts</h2>
      </>
    ) : null
  }

  <h2>Subscriptions</h2>
  <p>
    Subscriptions are billed in advance for the chosen period. You can cancel at
    any time; cancellation stops the next renewal and you keep access until the
    end of the period already paid for.
  </p>

  <h3>First 14 days</h3>
  <p>
    A first subscription can be refunded in full within 14 days of the initial
    charge, for any reason. Write to us and we will process it — you do not have
    to justify it.
  </p>

  <h3>After 14 days</h3>
  <p>
    Part-used periods are not refunded pro rata, with two exceptions:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>A sustained outage.</strong> If the service is unavailable for a
      material part of a billing period, we refund that part without being
      asked.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A charge you did not authorise.</strong> Refunded in full, and we
      will investigate how it happened.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Credits</h2>
  <p>
    Credits purchased separately are consumed on use and are not refundable once
    spent, because the GPU time they represent has been used.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Unused credits are refundable</strong> at the price paid, pro rata,
    for 90 days from purchase. Credits included with a subscription carry
    forward while the subscription is active but have no cash value.
  </p>

  <h2>Failed renders</h2>
  <p>
    A render or bake that fails through a fault on our side is refunded to your
    credit balance automatically. You do not need to ask, and it does not count
    against any cap.
  </p>
  <p>
    A render that completes but that you dislike is not a failure and is not
    refunded — the compute was spent producing exactly what was requested.
  </p>

  <h2>Enterprise agreements</h2>
  <p>
    Where a signed agreement exists, its terms take precedence over this page.
  </p>

  <h2>How to request a refund</h2>
  <p>
    Contact us through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> with the account
    email and, where relevant, the invoice or job reference. We aim to respond
    within two working days, and approved refunds are returned to the original
    payment method.
  </p>
</Legal>
